id:                     E492
trigger_tool:           meson|conan|ldso|readelf
phase:                  testing|packaging
error_signature:        Error loading shared library lib[^ ]+\\.so\\.0|NEEDED.*lib[^ ]+\\.so\\.0|lib[^ ]+\\.so\\.0.*symbol not found|meson test.*exit status 127

severity:               2
category:               meson, linking, packaging, runtime, testing
match_keywords:         zix, Meson, SONAME, build tree, install tree, libzix-0.so.0, Error loading shared library, LD_LIBRARY_PATH, shared library alias, OHOS
title:                  Materialize Meson shared-library aliases when OHOS does not expose SONAME names

root_cause:             Meson built the real versioned library, but the OHOS build/install tree did not expose the SONAME and developer-name aliases that the runtime loader and consumers search for. Adding only LD_LIBRARY_PATH is insufficient when the exact NEEDED filename is absent.
affected_scope:         Meson packages on HarmonyOS PC that build shared libraries named like libfoo.so.X.Y.Z while tests or consumers need libfoo.so.X or libfoo.so.
verification_cmd:       find <build>/ -name 'lib*.so*' -exec ls -l {} +; readelf -d <test-binary> | grep -E 'NEEDED|RUNPATH'; run meson test and Conan test_package with isolated runtime paths.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           build-and-package-soname-alias-materialization
rec_description:        After meson build and after meson install, ensure the real versioned shared library has the SONAME alias and developer alias in the relevant build or package lib directory. Prefer relative symlinks on capable filesystems and fall back to copying the real ELF when symlinks are denied.
rec_command:            ensure libfoo.so.X and libfoo.so exist next to libfoo.so.X.Y.Z before meson test and after install
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe-helper

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      configure-unversioned-shared-library-if-upstream-supports-it
fallback_description:   If the project supports disabling versioned SONAME layout without losing ABI information, configure an unversioned shared object and validate DT_NEEDED/SONAME explicitly.
fallback_command:       meson configure -Ddefault_library=shared; readelf -d libfoo.so
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          build-system-option

forbid_1_pattern:       LD_LIBRARY_PATH=.*only|prepend_path\\(\"LD_LIBRARY_PATH\"
forbid_1_reason:        Runtime search paths cannot load a missing SONAME filename; the required alias must exist.
forbid_1_consequence:   Meson tests or consumers still fail with Error loading shared library even though the directory is in LD_LIBRARY_PATH.
forbid_2_pattern:       copy only .*lib.*\\.so($| )
forbid_2_reason:        The loader resolves the exact NEEDED name, usually the SONAME alias, not only the developer library name.
forbid_2_consequence:   Link can pass while runtime execution fails after cache relocation or isolated testing.
forbid_3_pattern:       skip.*meson test|tests.*disabled
forbid_3_reason:        The failure is in runtime artifact layout, not in upstream test logic.
forbid_3_consequence:   A broad skip hides loader and packaging defects that consumers will hit.

principles:             P010, P012, P016

doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-zix-meson-build-tree-soname-alias.md
similar_to: E274, E316
last_updated:           2026-08-25
source_event:           zix 0.8.1 shadow CI: first runs failed with Error loading shared library libzix-0.so.0; final run passed after materializing build and package aliases
authors: wxjshr <wxjshr@noreply.gitcode.com>
source_pr: !6611
source_commit:

metrics_success_count:  1
metrics_fail_count:     2
metrics_confidence:     0.9
